\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Three published kernel counts}
\date{2026-11-12}

\p{For periods #{N_j\ge 3}, three published counts sit beside the
counting Laplacian of \ref{fdip-00OL}. The centered Dirac operator
of \ref{fdip-000T}, restated in the
[Dirac–Kähler operators](fdip-0091), has complex kernel dimension
#{2^{d+e}}, where #{e} counts the even periods. The symbol of
\ref{fdip-009R} vanishes at the #{2^d} corners. \ref{fdip-009V}
gives the kernel of the free Wilson operator at trivial links.
\ref{fdip-00OM} shows a counting Laplacian whose degree-zero
kernel has rank #{2} while the degree-zero Betti number is #{1}.
Over an ordered field, \ref{fdip-00OP} identifies the harmonic
space of a positive weight with the cohomology, and
\ref{fdip-00OQ} gives both the rank #{2^d}.}
